{"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","body":"Second repro, same repo: after repairing the DB by hand (relinked 2 children, 4 depends_on, re-deleted 2 tickets), ti sync output was: Pull: 2 new ticket(s) (the two deleted ones), Pull: 4 updated ticket(s) (the map and the tickets whose links/comments I had repaired), Push: 53 ticket(s) synced. Afterwards refs/meta/local/main and the remote ref were both unchanged (ea6a4b4...), so nothing local was pushed, and the pull reverted every local repair: map children back to 16, deleted tickets back, their tombstones gone, sync_state advanced. So pull appears to overwrite local state with the remote tree rather than merge it, and local edits made after the last sync are neither pushed nor kept. Workaround used: restore a copy of .git/git-meta.sqlite taken before the sync. Do not run ti sync in a repo with unsynced local changes until this is fixed."}